00:27:51,790 --> 00:27:53,750
One, two, three.

303
00:27:55,460 --> 00:27:57,550
- You can't do that. - What?

304
00:27:57,630 --> 00:27:59,090
Can they do that?

305
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:06,010
the boat for the mainland will be leaving at 1900.

306
00:28:06,100 --> 00:28:11,020
All personnel be at the dock no later than 1845. No exceptions.

307
00:28:11,810 --> 00:28:14,940
Good day, Henry. Good day, sir.

308
00:28:28,990 --> 00:28:30,580
It's turning the eggs.

309
00:28:34,170 --> 00:28:38,300
Perfect timing. I'd hoped they'd hatch before I had to go to the boat.

310
00:28:38,380 --> 00:28:40,840
Henry, why didn't you tell me?

311
00:28:41,050 --> 00:28:44,970
I insist on being here when they're born.

312
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:48,100
Come on.

313
00:28:49,640 --> 00:28:51,310
Come on, little one.

314
00:28:57,650 --> 00:28:59,020
Come on, then.

315
00:29:02,360 --> 00:29:04,200
Very good. Push.

316
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:08,330
- Very good. - God.

317
00:29:08,410 --> 00:29:10,830
Push. Come on.

318
00:29:11,410 --> 00:29:14,330
Come on. Come on, then.

319
00:29:14,620 --> 00:29:17,460
There you are.

320
00:29:22,510 --> 00:29:25,880
They imprint on the first creature they come in contact with.

321
00:29:25,970 --> 00:29:28,890
That's it. Helps them to trust me.

322
00:29:29,680 --> 00:29:34,520
I've been present for the birth of every little creature on this island.

323
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:38,810
Surely not the ones that have bred in the wild?

324
00:29:38,980 --> 00:29:41,230
Actually they can't breed in the wild.

325
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:44,150
Population control is one of our security precautions.

326
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:47,200
