spitting its venom at its prey, causing blindness and paralysis,

500
00:42:22,370 --> 00:42:25,460
allowing the carnivore to eat at its leisure.

501
00:42:26,120 --> 00:42:29,790
This makes Dilophosaurus a beautiful but deadly addition

502
00:42:29,960 --> 00:42:31,790
to Jurassic Park.

503
00:42:38,970 --> 00:42:40,470
Alan?

504
00:42:41,550 --> 00:42:42,720
Where?

505
00:42:46,600 --> 00:42:47,770
Damn.

506
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:54,730
Vehicle headlights are on and not responding.

507
00:42:54,820 --> 00:42:57,320
Those shouldn't be running off of car batteries.

508
00:42:57,450 --> 00:42:59,990
Item 151 on today's glitch list.

509
00:43:00,110 --> 00:43:03,240
We have all the problems of a major theme park and a major zoo

510
00:43:03,330 --> 00:43:06,330
and the computers aren't even on their feet yet.

511
00:43:08,250 --> 00:43:12,000
Dennis, our lives are in your hands and you have butterfingers?

512
00:43:13,670 --> 00:43:16,090
I am totally unappreciated in my time.

513
00:43:16,300 --> 00:43:20,090
You can run this park from this room with minimal staff for up to three days.

514
00:43:20,180 --> 00:43:24,180
You think that kind of automation is easy? Or cheap?

515
00:43:24,510 --> 00:43:27,060
You know anybody who can network eight machines

516
00:43:27,140 --> 00:43:30,940
and de-bug two million lines of code on my salary? If so, I want to see them.

517
00:43:31,020 --> 00:43:35,440
Sorry about your financial problems, I really am. But they are your problems.

518
00:43:35,530 --> 00:43:38,360
You're absolutely right. Everything's my problem.

519
00:43:38,440 --> 00:43:42,700
I will not be drawn into another financial debate with you.

520
00:43:42,780 --> 00:43:43,950
I really will not.

521
00:43:44,030 --> 00:43:46,080
There's been hardly any debate at all.

522
00:43:46,160 --> 00:43:49,040
I don't blame people for their mistakes.

523
00:43:49,660 --> 00:43:51,870
But I do ask that they pay for them.

524
00:43:52,120 --> 00:43:53,330
Thanks, Dad.

525
00:43:54,460 --> 00:43:55,630
The headlights.

526
00:43:55,710 --> 00:43:58,300
I'll debug the tour program when they get back, okay?

527
00:43:58,380 --> 00:44:01,720
It'll eat a lot of compute cycles. We'll lose part of the system.

528
00:44:01,720 --> 00:44:04,970
There's a finite amount of memory, you can't use it for everything.

529
00:44:05,050 --> 00:44:08,680
Are you gonna compile for a half an hour... Quiet, all of you!

530
00:44:09,680 --> 00:44:12,060
They're approaching the Tyrannosaur paddock.

531
00:45:03,070 --> 00:45:06,620
God creates dinosaurs. God destroys dinosaurs.

532
00:45:07,070 --> 00:45:11,870
God creates man. Man destroys God. Man creates dinosaurs.

533
00:45:12,960 --> 00:45:16,630
Dinosaurs eat man.

534
00:45:18,090 --> 00:45:20,130
Woman inherits the earth.

535
00:45:27,760 --> 00:45:30,970
- We'll try to tempt the Rex now. - Keep watching the fence.

536
00:45:41,110 --> 00:45:43,320
What's going to happen to the goat?

537
00:45:47,320 --> 00:45:49,160
He's going to eat the goat?

538
00:45:49,330 --> 00:45:50,740
Excellent.

539
00:45:51,830 --> 00:45:55,080
What's the matter, kid? You never had lamb chops?

540
00:45:55,670 --> 00:45:57,960
I happen to be a vegetarian.

541
00:46:06,300 --> 00:46:09,510
T-Rex doesn't want to be fed. He wants to hunt.

542
00:46:10,430 --> 00:46:15,180
You can't just suppress 65 million years of gut instinct.

543
00:46:37,120 --> 00:46:42,040
Eventually you do plan to have dinosaurs on your dinosaur tour, right?

544
00:46:45,720 --> 00:46:48,050
Hello. Yes?

545
00:46:48,630 --> 00:46:50,640
I really hate that man.

546
00:46:55,850 --> 00:47:00,650
The Tyrannosaur doesn't obey any set patterns or park schedules.

547
00:47:00,730 --> 00:47:02,900
The essence of chaos.

548
00:47:04,070 --> 00:47:06,070
I'm still not clear on chaos.

549
00:47:07,740 --> 00:47:11,660
It simply deals with unpredictability in complex systems.

550
00:47:13,200 --> 00:47:15,160
The shorthand is the Butterfly Effect.

551
00:47:15,240 --> 00:47:17,500
A butterfly can flap its wings in Peking

552
00:47:17,580 --> 00:47:20,670
and in Central Park you get rain instead of sunshine.

553
00:47:22,880 --> 00:47:24,750
Was I going too fast? I missed it.

554
00:47:24,880 --> 00:47:26,010
I did a fly-by.

555
00:47:26,090 --> 00:47:28,840
Give me that glass of water. We'll conduct an experiment.

556
00:47:28,920 --> 00:47:32,600
We should be still. The car's bouncing. That's okay. It's just an example.

557
00:47:32,720 --> 00:47:35,100
Put your hand flat like a hieroglyphic.

558
00:47:35,680 --> 00:47:37,600
A drop of water falls on your hand.

559
00:47:37,680 --> 00:47:40,440
Which way will the drop roll off? Which finger?

560
00:47:40,730 --> 00:47:42,190
Thumb, I'd say.

561
00:47:44,900 --> 00:47:46,940
Freeze your hand. Don't move.

562
00:47:47,030 --> 00:47:49,950
I'll do the same thing, start with the same place again.

563
00:47:50,030 --> 00:47:51,450
Which way, now?

564
00:47:51,570 --> 00:47:54,530
Let's say back the same way.

565
00:47:56,910 --> 00:47:59,290
It changed. Why?

566
00:47:59,460 --> 00:48:01,750
Because tiny variations,

567
00:48:02,290 --> 00:48:04,710
the orientation of the hairs on your hands...

568
00:48:04,790 --> 00:48:06,130
Alan, look at this.

569
00:48:06,210 --> 00:48:09,880
...the amount of blood distending your vessels, imperfections in the skin...

570
00:48:09,970 --> 00:48:12,890
"Imperfections in the skin"? ...just microscopic,

571
00:48:12,970 --> 00:48:15,890
never repeat and vastly affect the outcome.

572
00:48:15,970 --> 00:48:18,310
That's what? Unpredictability.

573
00:48:21,140 --> 00:48:24,310
There. Look at this. See? I'm right again.

574
00:48:24,400 --> 00:48:28,820
Nobody could predict that Dr. Grant would suddenly jump out of a moving vehicle.

575
00:48:30,990 --> 00:48:33,410
And there's another example.

576
00:48:34,910 --> 00:48:39,330
See, here I am now by myself, talking to myself. That's Chaos Theory.

577
00:48:40,750 --> 00:48:43,670
Stop the program.

578
00:48:45,670 --> 00:48:50,050
I told you, how many times, we needed locking mechanisms on the vehicle doors.

579
00:48:50,130 --> 00:48:52,760
Stopping park vehicles and rebooting program.

580
00:48:52,840 --> 00:48:55,090
We're on. Will notify for resume.

581
00:48:57,510 --> 00:48:59,600
I'll switch it over to TelePrompTer.

582
00:48:59,680 --> 00:49:03,350
What about the circuit integrities? Screen says faulty sensor.

583
00:49:05,690 --> 00:49:09,190
I'll call security. We're at full go on that and it looks good.

584
00:49:09,480 --> 00:49:12,990
Like I said, there's this other book by a guy named Bakker

585
00:49:13,070 --> 00:49:15,320
and he says dinosaurs died from diseases.

586
00:49:15,410 --> 00:49:18,410
Where are we going? He didn't say they turned into birds.

587
00:49:18,490 --> 00:49:20,700
Anyone else think we shouldn't be out here?

588
00:49:20,790 --> 00:49:23,960
And his book was a lot fatter than yours. Like this.

589
00:49:24,040 --> 00:49:26,790
Really? Yours was fully illustrated.

590
00:49:27,840 --> 00:49:29,170
You okay?

591
00:49:29,300 --> 00:49:31,670
Look at this. Wait. Watch.

592
00:49:32,380 --> 00:49:34,220
Come on. Watch this.

593
00:49:36,180 --> 00:49:37,680
Whoa.

594
00:49:39,970 --> 00:49:41,520
Everybody stay here.

595
00:49:56,740 --> 00:49:57,910
Wow.

596
00:49:59,740 --> 00:50:01,910
Okay? Of course.

597
00:50:04,870 --> 00:50:08,670
- Don't be scared. - Come on, it's okay. Muldoon tranquillized her for me.

598
00:50:08,750 --> 00:50:10,090
She's sick.

599
00:50:18,930 --> 00:50:20,390
Oh, my God.

600
00:50:35,900 --> 00:50:37,450
Hey, baby.

601
00:50:42,950 --> 00:50:45,450
She was always my favorite when I was a kid

602
00:50:45,540 --> 00:50:48,920
and now I see she's the most beautiful thing I ever saw.

603
00:50:53,250 --> 00:50:54,630
It's okay.

604
00:50:57,760 --> 00:51:00,300
Microvesicles. That's interesting.

605
00:51:02,300 --> 00:51:04,640
Thanks. What are her symptoms?

606
00:51:05,220 --> 00:51:07,980
Imbalance, disorientation, labored breathing.

607
00:51:08,140 --> 00:51:10,310
It seems to happen every six weeks or so.

608
00:51:10,400 --> 00:51:11,770
Six weeks.

609
00:51:25,410 --> 00:51:27,000
These are dilated. They are?

610
00:51:27,120 --> 00:51:30,080
Take a look. I'll be damned.

611
00:51:30,580 --> 00:51:34,340
That's pharmacological. From local plant life.

612
00:51:41,760 --> 00:51:43,890
Is this West Indian lilac?

613
00:51:44,350 --> 00:51:47,890
Yes. We know they're toxic, but the animals don't eat them.

614
00:51:52,310 --> 00:51:55,150
Are you sure? Pretty sure.

615
00:51:56,650 --> 00:51:58,900
There's only one way to be positive.

616
00:51:59,570 --> 00:52:02,110
I'd have to see the dinosaur's droppings.

617
00:52:03,280 --> 00:52:06,410
Dino droppings? Droppings?

618
00:52:12,210 --> 00:52:14,460
Yeah, I got that.

619
00:52:15,670 --> 00:52:18,800
That storm center hasn't dissipated or changed course.

620
00:52:18,920 --> 00:52:21,380
We're gonna have to cut the tour short.

621
00:52:21,470 --> 00:52:23,260
We'll pick it up again tomorrow.

622
00:52:23,340 --> 00:52:26,600
Are you sure we have to? It's not worth taking the chance.

623
00:52:26,680 --> 00:52:30,310
Sustained winds at 45 knots. Tell them when they get back in the cars.

624
00:52:30,390 --> 00:52:35,060
Ladies and gentlemen, last shuttle leaving for the dock leaves in five minutes.

625
00:52:35,150 --> 00:52:37,480
Drop what you're doing and leave now.

626
00:52:39,610 --> 00:52:40,900
Damn!

627
00:52:48,580 --> 00:52:50,500
That is one big pile of shit.

628
00:52:57,840 --> 00:53:00,460
You're right. There's no trace of lilac berries.

629
00:53:00,550 --> 00:53:02,590
That's so odd, though.

630
00:53:03,050 --> 00:53:06,680
All right, she's suffering from Melia toxicity

631
00:53:08,390 --> 00:53:10,680
every six weeks.

632
00:53:12,310 --> 00:53:15,850
Let's see, rats.

633
00:53:16,810 --> 00:53:19,980
She's tenacious.

634
00:53:20,900 --> 00:53:22,610
You have no idea.

635
00:53:24,700 --> 00:53:28,450
You will remember to wash your hands before you eat anything?

636
00:53:40,840 --> 00:53:44,760
Doctors, if you please, I have to insist that we get moving.

637
00:53:47,180 --> 00:53:50,760
I'd like to stay with Dr. Harding and finish up with the Trike.

638
00:53:51,520 --> 00:53:53,310
Sure. I'm in a gas-powered jeep.

639
00:53:53,390 --> 00:53:56,150
I'll drop her off at the center before I make the boat.

640
00:53:56,230 --> 00:53:58,940
Great. Then I'll catch up with you later.

641
00:53:59,020 --> 00:54:00,150
You sure?

642
00:54:00,230 --> 00:54:02,990
Yeah, I want to stay with her a little longer.

643
00:54:03,070 --> 00:54:04,490
Okay, then.

644
00:54:19,290 --> 00:54:23,590
There's nothing I can do. The captain says we got to go, we got to go.

645
00:54:23,670 --> 00:54:25,380
You've got to give me the time.

646
00:54:25,470 --> 00:54:28,930
I did a test run, it took me 20 minutes. I think I can push it to 18

647
00:54:29,010 --> 00:54:31,350
but you've got to give me at least 15 minutes.

648
00:54:31,430 --> 00:54:32,760
No promises.

649
00:54:40,520 --> 00:54:43,230
Visitor vehicles are returning to the garage.

650
00:54:45,610 --> 00:54:50,450
So much for our first tour. Two no-shows and one sick Triceratops.

651
00:54:51,870 --> 00:54:53,580
It could've been worse.

652
00:54:54,790 --> 00:54:56,040
A lot worse.

653
00:54:56,210 --> 00:55:00,290
- Anybody want a soda or something? - I'm going up to the machine.

654
00:55:00,380 --> 00:55:02,540
I thought maybe I'd get somebody something.

655
00:55:02,630 --> 00:55:06,380
I've had only sweets and I'm gonna get something salty.

656
00:55:07,220 --> 00:55:09,640
I finished debugging the phones.

657
00:55:10,720 --> 00:55:12,810
I was going to, so I did.

658
00:55:13,060 --> 00:55:16,060
So I debugged the phones. And I thought maybe

659
00:55:16,180 --> 00:55:18,890
I should tell you the system will be compiling

660
00:55:19,020 --> 00:55:21,900
for 18 to 20 minutes, so some of the minor systems,

661
00:55:21,980 --> 00:55:25,900
they might go on and off for a while, but it's nothing to worry about.

662
00:55:48,090 --> 00:55:52,510
Do you got any kids? Me? Hell, yeah. Three. I love kids.

663
00:55:54,300 --> 00:55:56,680
Anything at all can and does happen.

664
00:55:57,180 --> 00:55:59,690
Same with wives, for that matter.

665
00:56:00,100 --> 00:56:02,560
You're married? Occasionally.

666
00:56:04,610 --> 00:56:08,990
I'm always on the lookout for a future ex-Mrs. Malcolm.

667
00:56:22,540 --> 00:56:25,790
Five, four, three,

668
00:56:27,750 --> 00:56:28,800
two, one.

669
00:56:37,140 --> 00:56:39,390
- That's odd. - What?

670
00:56:39,640 --> 00:56:42,060
Door security systems are shutting down.

671
00:56:42,140 --> 00:56:45,400
Nedry said a few systems would go off-line, didn't he?

672
00:57:41,540 --> 00:57:43,660
By the way, Dr. Sattler,

673
00:57:44,540 --> 00:57:47,960
she's not available, is she? Why?

674
00:57:50,880 --> 00:57:54,130
I'm sorry. You two are... Yeah.

675
00:57:57,050 --> 00:58:00,810
What'd I touch? You didn't touch anything. We stopped.

676
00:58:09,900 --> 00:58:11,400
What the hell?

677
00:58:11,480 --> 00:58:14,490
What now? Fences are failing all over the park.

678
00:58:14,900 --> 00:58:17,070
Find Nedry. Check the vending machines.

679
00:58:49,270 --> 00:58:51,020
Just look at this work station.

680
00:58:51,110 --> 00:58:54,740
What a complete slob. The Raptor fences aren't out, are they?

681
00:59:01,620 --> 00:59:03,410
No, no. They're still on.

682
00:59:06,040 --> 00:59:08,540
Why the hell would he turn the other ones off?

683
00:59:48,660 --> 00:59:50,330
Access main program.

684
00:59:51,170 --> 00:59:52,830
Access main security.

685
00:59:53,590 --> 00:59:55,670
Access main program grid.

686
01:00:04,430 --> 01:00:06,520
You didn't say the magic word.

687
01:00:06,930 --> 01:00:10,480
Please! God damn it. I hate this hacker crap.

688
01:00:10,600 --> 01:00:14,020
Phone Nedry's people in Cambridge.

689
01:00:16,270 --> 01:00:17,820
Phones are out, too.

690
01:00:21,360 --> 01:00:23,280
Where did the vehicles stop?

691
01:00:44,180 --> 01:00:45,890
Their radio's out, too.

692
01:00:46,220 --> 01:00:48,560
Gennaro said to stay put. Kids okay?

693
01:00:48,640 --> 01:00:50,810
I didn't ask. Why wouldn't they be?

694
01:00:50,890 --> 01:00:52,560
Kids get scared. What's scary?

695
01:00:52,690 --> 01:00:55,810
It's just a little hiccup in the power. I'm not scared.

696
01:00:55,900 --> 01:00:58,230
I didn't say you were scared. I know.

697
01:00:58,980 --> 01:01:00,320
Boo!

698
01:01:01,570 --> 01:01:03,910
Hey, where did you find those?

699
01:01:04,070 --> 01:01:06,740
In the box, under my seat. Are they heavy?

700
01:01:06,950 --> 01:01:09,620
Yeah. Then they're expensive. Put them back.

701
01:01:16,840 --> 01:01:18,420
Don't scare me.

702
01:01:29,970 --> 01:01:31,770
Cool. Night vision.

703
01:01:57,250 --> 01:01:58,670
Did you feel that?

704
01:02:32,660 --> 01:02:35,290
Maybe it's the power trying to come back on.

705
01:02:37,870 --> 01:02:39,170
What is that?

706
01:02:56,100 --> 01:02:57,480
Where's the goat?

707
01:03:20,750 --> 01:03:22,000
Jesus!

708
01:03:26,670 --> 01:03:28,470
He left us.

709
01:03:39,940 --> 01:03:44,270
Where does he think he's going? When you got to go, you got to go.

710
01:04:02,420 --> 01:04:03,710
Dr. Grant.

711
01:04:16,600 --> 01:04:18,730
I hate being right all the time.

712
01:04:27,780 --> 01:04:31,950
Keep absolutely still. Its vision is based on movement.

713
01:04:46,340 --> 01:04:47,920
Turn the light off.

714
01:04:52,800 --> 01:04:54,300
Turn the light off!

715
01:05:50,150 --> 01:05:53,030
Hurry! Turn it off! I'm sorry!

716
01:05:57,200 --> 01:05:59,200
You're the one who turned it...

717
01:07:17,990 --> 01:07:19,320
Ian, freeze!

718
01:07:19,820 --> 01:07:21,280
Get the kids!

719
01:07:22,200 --> 01:07:24,540
Get rid of the flare! Get the kids!

720
01:07:25,540 --> 01:07:27,120
Get rid of the flare!

721
01:07:30,120 --> 01:07:31,630
Hail Mary, full of grace...

722
01:07:49,310 --> 01:07:50,480
No!

723
01:07:54,360 --> 01:07:55,650
Dr. Grant!

724
01:08:00,240 --> 01:08:02,820
I'm stuck. The seat's got my feet.

725
01:08:02,910 --> 01:08:05,200
I'll get you next. You're okay.

726
01:08:06,580 --> 01:08:08,000
You're all right.

727
01:08:08,710 --> 01:08:10,330
Tim!

728
01:08:14,000 --> 01:08:16,920
Don't move. He can't see us if we don't move.

729
01:09:22,320 --> 01:09:24,410
Lex, you're choking me.

730
01:09:27,240 --> 01:09:28,490
Grab the wire.

731
01:09:48,260 --> 01:09:52,140
"Keycheck space minus 0. Keychecks off, safety space minus 0."

732
01:09:52,270 --> 01:09:55,440
He's turning the safety systems off. Doesn't want anybody to see.

733
01:09:55,520 --> 01:09:58,820
Look at this next entry. It's the kicker. "White rabbit object."

734
01:09:58,940 --> 01:10:02,860
It did it all. With the keychecks off, the computer didn't file the keystrokes.

735
01:10:02,940 --> 01:10:06,700
The way to find them is to check the computer's lines of code one by one.

736
01:10:06,780 --> 01:10:09,950
How many lines of code are there? About two million.

737
01:10:10,200 --> 01:10:11,700
Two million? Yeah.

738
01:10:14,620 --> 01:10:19,290
Robert, I wonder if perhaps you would be good enough to take a gas jeep

739
01:10:20,880 --> 01:10:23,130
and bring back my grandchildren.

740
01:10:24,010 --> 01:10:25,170
Sure.

741
01:10:27,970 --> 01:10:29,470
I'm going with him.

742
01:10:32,810 --> 01:10:33,980
John.

743
01:10:39,810 --> 01:10:43,530
I can't get Jurassic Park back online without Dennis Nedry.

744
01:10:46,450 --> 01:10:48,070
Should have been there by now.

745
01:11:03,340 --> 01:11:04,670
Damn it!

746
01:11:11,350 --> 01:11:12,760
There's the road!

747
01:11:19,350 --> 01:11:23,360
Winch this sucker off the thing and then I tie it to that thing there.

748
01:11:23,440 --> 01:11:26,860
I'll pull down this thing here, and pull it back up again.

749
01:11:35,200 --> 01:11:38,620
My glasses. I can afford more glasses!

750
01:12:07,820 --> 01:12:11,160
You've got time. You can do it. Do it. Come on, Dennis.

751
01:12:18,580 --> 01:12:19,790
Hello.

752
01:12:24,750 --> 01:12:27,550
Yeah, that's nice. I've got to go.

753
01:12:38,770 --> 01:12:40,100
Nice boy.

754
01:12:42,190 --> 01:12:43,810
Nice dinosaur.

755
01:12:44,650 --> 01:12:48,070
Thought you were one of your big brothers. You're not so bad.

756
01:12:48,150 --> 01:12:52,070
What do you want? A little food? Look at me. I just fell down a hill.

757
01:12:52,150 --> 01:12:55,660
I'm soaking wet. I don't have any food. I have nothing on me.

758
01:12:57,290 --> 01:12:59,450
Go on. Play fetch?

759
01:13:01,410 --> 01:13:02,620
Look, stick.

760
01:13:04,290 --> 01:13:06,460
Look at stick.

761
01:13:07,130 --> 01:13:10,300
Stick, stupid. Fetch the stick, boy. Look at the stick.

762
01:13:10,800 --> 01:13:13,130
You like the stick? Go on and get it.

763
01:13:13,300 --> 01:13:15,140
No wonder you're extinct.

764
01:13:16,390 --> 01:13:19,060
I'm gonna run you over when I come back down.

765
01:14:35,090 --> 01:14:36,680
Timmy!

766
01:14:40,760 --> 01:14:42,810
Now, Lex. Listen.

767
01:14:43,520 --> 01:14:45,180
Lex, I'm right here.

768
01:14:45,850 --> 01:14:48,350
I'll look after you. I have to help your brother.

769
01:14:48,440 --> 01:14:50,650
Stay right here and wait for me.

770
01:14:51,020 --> 01:14:53,360
He left us.

771
01:14:53,860 --> 01:14:56,360
But that's not what I'm going to do.

772
01:14:58,410 --> 01:14:59,570
Okay?

773
01:15:02,030 --> 01:15:03,160
Stay here.

774
01:15:30,400 --> 01:15:32,310
You hear me? I'm coming up.

775
01:15:33,020 --> 01:15:36,990
I hate climbing. I hate trees, way too high.

776
01:16:05,260 --> 01:16:06,350
You okay?

777
01:16:09,350 --> 01:16:10,600
I threw up.

778
01:16:13,730 --> 01:16:14,940
That's okay.

779
01:16:15,900 --> 01:16:17,610
Just give me your hand.

780
01:16:21,780 --> 01:16:25,830
Tim, I won't tell anyone you threw up. Just give me your hand.

781
01:16:34,880 --> 01:16:36,380
Here, I've got you.

782
01:16:38,010 --> 01:16:39,170
Okay.

783
01:16:39,590 --> 01:16:43,430
That's good. Over the rail. Don't pull me too hard.

784
01:16:47,970 --> 01:16:50,230
- Stand on the door. - Hang on to me.

785
01:16:53,850 --> 01:16:56,570
That's not too bad, right, Timmy? Yes, it is.

786
01:16:56,650 --> 01:16:59,360
It's like a tree house. Your dad ever build you one?

787
01:16:59,440 --> 01:17:00,990
No. Yeah, me, too.

788
01:17:02,660 --> 01:17:05,450
The thing about climbing is, you never look down.

789
01:17:05,530 --> 01:17:07,120
This is impossible.

790
01:17:07,410 --> 01:17:11,960
How am I going to do this? It's about... I'm going to help you with your footing.

791
01:17:15,750 --> 01:17:16,880
Oh, no.

792
01:17:17,420 --> 01:17:18,710
Tim, go.

793
01:17:41,070 --> 01:17:42,530
Go, Tim, go!

794
01:17:50,830 --> 01:17:52,040
Faster, Tim!

795
01:17:58,750 --> 01:17:59,880
Tim, jump!

796
01:18:03,880 --> 01:18:04,970
Go, Tim.

797
01:18:13,430 --> 01:18:15,850
We're back in the car again.

798
01:18:18,060 --> 01:18:20,150
At least you're out of the tree.

799
01:18:25,530 --> 01:18:27,990
Where's the other car?

800
01:18:30,410 --> 01:18:31,580
Alan!

801
01:18:32,700 --> 01:18:33,950
Dr. Grant!

802
01:18:50,100 --> 01:18:53,520
I think this was Gennaro. I think this was, too.

803
01:18:57,100 --> 01:18:59,650
I think it's ahead of us. It could be anywhere.

804
01:18:59,730 --> 01:19:03,110
With fences down, it can wander in and out of any paddock it likes.

805
01:19:10,120 --> 01:19:12,120
He's put a tourniquet on. Ian.

806
01:19:13,830 --> 01:19:16,540
Remind me to thank John for a lovely weekend.

807
01:19:21,540 --> 01:19:23,300
Can we chance moving him?

808
01:19:24,630 --> 01:19:26,090
Please chance it.

809
01:19:34,640 --> 01:19:36,230
Ellie, come on!

810
01:19:43,770 --> 01:19:45,030
It's the other car!

811
01:19:45,610 --> 01:19:46,860
Dr. Grant?

812
01:19:51,370 --> 01:19:52,870
They're not here.

813
01:20:22,230 --> 01:20:23,730
Anybody hear that?

814
01:20:27,320 --> 01:20:29,740
It's an impact tremor, is what it is.

815
01:20:30,610 --> 01:20:32,410
I'm fairly alarmed here.

816
01:20:33,870 --> 01:20:37,580
Come on. We've got to get out of here. Now! Right now!

817
01:20:38,370 --> 01:20:39,460
Let's go.

818
01:20:50,920 --> 01:20:52,220
Must go faster.

819
01:20:54,890 --> 01:20:57,720
Here it comes! Stand on it! Fifth gear!

820
01:21:04,060 --> 01:21:07,190
Get off the stick! Bloody move! Look out!

821
01:21:34,300 --> 01:21:36,640
Think they'll have that on the tour?

822
01:21:44,810 --> 01:21:46,400
Are you hearing this?

823
01:21:52,990 --> 01:21:55,160
- Come on, Tim. - Hurry up.

824
01:21:56,120 --> 01:21:57,830
Let's get up this tree.

825
01:22:00,790 --> 01:22:03,540
Come on, Tim, it's okay. Listen. Try up here.

826
01:22:05,370 --> 01:22:06,630
Oh, man.

827
01:22:07,880 --> 01:22:09,210
I hate trees.

828
01:22:09,750 --> 01:22:13,380
They don't bother me. Yeah? Well, you weren't in the last one.

829
01:22:28,020 --> 01:22:31,570
Look at the Brontosauruses. I mean, Brachiosaurus.

830
01:22:33,110 --> 01:22:34,530
They're singing.

831
01:23:03,560 --> 01:23:05,600
Don't let the monsters come over here.

832
01:23:05,680 --> 01:23:09,100
They're not monsters, they're animals. These are herbivores.

833
01:23:09,350 --> 01:23:12,730
They only eat vegetables. For you, I think they'd make an exception.

834
01:23:12,820 --> 01:23:14,480
I hate the other kind.

835
01:23:16,570 --> 01:23:19,360
They just do what they do.

836
01:23:39,470 --> 01:23:40,680
What's that?

837
01:23:45,890 --> 01:23:49,850
What are you and Ellie going to do now, if you don't dig up bones anymore?

838
01:23:51,270 --> 01:23:52,520
I don't know.

839
01:23:53,770 --> 01:23:56,190
I guess we'll just have to evolve, too.

840
01:23:59,860 --> 01:24:02,070
What do you call a blind dinosaur?

841
01:24:04,080 --> 01:24:08,080
What do you call a blind dinosaur? "Do-you-think-he-saurus."

842
01:24:11,790 --> 01:24:14,290
What do you call a blind dinosaur's dog?

843
01:24:15,130 --> 01:24:16,460
You got me.

844
01:24:16,630 --> 01:24:18,720
A "Do-you-think -he-saurus rex."

845
01:24:21,300 --> 01:24:23,470
Alan? Yeah?

846
01:24:24,140 --> 01:24:27,310
What if the dinosaurs come back while we're all asleep?

847
01:24:29,640 --> 01:24:31,810
I'll stay awake. All night?

848
01:24:34,440 --> 01:24:35,570
All night.

849
01:25:25,820 --> 01:25:27,450
They were all melting.

850
01:25:31,160 --> 01:25:34,290
Malcolm's okay for now. I gave him a shot of morphine.

851
01:25:38,170 --> 01:25:39,710
They'll be fine.

852
01:25:40,710 --> 01:25:45,010
Who better to get the children through Jurassic Park than a dinosaur expert?

853
01:25:49,470 --> 01:25:51,220
You know, the first

854
01:25:52,520 --> 01:25:55,980
attraction I ever built when I came down from Scotland

855
01:25:57,650 --> 01:26:00,150
was a flea circus, Petticoat Lane.

856
01:26:01,530 --> 01:26:03,320
Really quite wonderful.

857
01:26:03,900 --> 01:26:07,160
I had a wee trapeze and a

858
01:26:10,370 --> 01:26:11,580
carousel

859
01:26:15,500 --> 01:26:16,920
and a seesaw.

860
01:26:18,040 --> 01:26:20,250
They all move motorized, of course.

861
01:26:20,590 --> 01:26:23,260
People said they saw the fleas. "I can see the fleas.

862
01:26:23,380 --> 01:26:25,090
"Can't you see the fleas?"

863
01:26:25,880 --> 01:26:30,180
Clown fleas, high-wire fleas, and fleas on parade.

864
01:26:36,400 --> 01:26:37,850
With this place,

865
01:26:39,940 --> 01:26:43,360
I wanted to show them something that wasn't an illusion.

866
01:26:44,360 --> 01:26:47,450
Something that was real. Something that they could

867
01:26:50,620 --> 01:26:52,080
see and touch.

868
01:26:56,790 --> 01:26:59,250
An aim not devoid of merit.

869
01:27:03,760 --> 01:27:07,380
But you can't think through this one, John. You have to feel it.

870
01:27:09,590 --> 01:27:11,300
You're absolutely right.

871
01:27:13,140 --> 01:27:15,480
Hiring Nedry was a mistake, that's obvious.

872
01:27:15,560 --> 01:27:18,230
We're over-dependent on automation, I can see that now.

873
01:27:18,310 --> 01:27:20,980
Next time, everything's correctable.

874
01:27:21,770 --> 01:27:24,990
Creation is an act of sheer will.

875
01:27:27,320 --> 01:27:29,280
Next time, it'll be flawless.

876
01:27:29,820 --> 01:27:33,160
It's still the flea circus. It's all an illusion.

877
01:27:33,330 --> 01:27:34,830
When we have control...

878
01:27:34,910 --> 01:27:37,580
You've never had control! That's the illusion.

879
01:27:37,750 --> 01:27:40,420
I was overwhelmed by the power of this place.

880
01:27:41,840 --> 01:27:43,250
I made a mistake, too.

881
01:27:43,340 --> 01:27:47,170
I didn't have enough respect for that power, and it's out now.

882
01:27:49,800 --> 01:27:52,970
The only thing that matters now are the people we love.

883
01:27:55,140 --> 01:27:57,270
Alan and Lex and Tim.

884
01:27:58,850 --> 01:28:02,020
John, they're out there, where people are dying.

885
01:28:19,040 --> 01:28:20,210
It's good.

886
01:28:24,170 --> 01:28:25,630
Spared no expense.

887
01:28:52,990 --> 01:28:56,160
Go away! It's okay. It's a Brachiosaurus.

888
01:28:56,830 --> 01:28:59,500
It's a "Veggie-saurus", Lex. "Veggie-saurus."

889
01:29:00,040 --> 01:29:01,250
Veggie.

890
01:29:02,170 --> 01:29:03,920
Come on. Come on, girl.

891
01:29:08,170 --> 01:29:09,550
Come on, baby.

892
01:29:13,010 --> 01:29:14,430
Go.

893
01:29:15,930 --> 01:29:17,430
I'm not letting go.

894
01:29:29,400 --> 01:29:32,240
It looks like it has a cold. Yeah. Maybe.

895
01:29:32,610 --> 01:29:34,240
Can I touch it? Sure.

896
01:29:34,570 --> 01:29:37,620
Just think of it as kind of a big cow.

897
01:29:40,950 --> 01:29:42,210
I like cows.

898
01:29:52,260 --> 01:29:54,590
Come on, girl. Come on up here, girl.

899
01:30:02,020 --> 01:30:03,310
God bless you.

900
01:30:08,650 --> 01:30:12,690
- Yuck. - Great. Now she'll never try anything new.

901
01:30:13,150 --> 01:30:16,160
She'll sit in her room, never come out, play on her computer.

902
01:30:16,280 --> 01:30:19,030
I'm a hacker. That's what I said. You're a nerd.

903
01:30:19,160 --> 01:30:22,370
I am not a computer nerd. I prefer to be called a hacker.

904
01:30:22,620 --> 01:30:23,830
God.

905
01:30:28,670 --> 01:30:30,340
You know what this is?

906
01:30:32,210 --> 01:30:34,220
It's a dinosaur egg.

907
01:30:34,970 --> 01:30:38,180
The dinosaurs are breeding.

908
01:30:41,350 --> 01:30:45,390
But my grandpa said all the dinosaurs were girls.

909
01:30:46,810 --> 01:30:49,020
Amphibian DNA. What's that?

910
01:30:50,820 --> 01:30:52,860
Well, on the tour,

911
01:30:53,070 --> 01:30:57,860
the film said they used frog DNA to fill in the gene-sequence gaps.

912
01:30:58,030 --> 01:31:01,370
They mutated the dinosaur genetic code

913
01:31:02,370 --> 01:31:04,660
and blended it with that of frogs.

914
01:31:07,540 --> 01:31:12,000
Some West African frogs have been known to change sex from male to female

915
01:31:12,090 --> 01:31:14,170
in a single sex environment.

916
01:31:16,050 --> 01:31:17,550
Malcolm was right.

917
01:31:19,090 --> 01:31:20,260
Look.

918
01:31:28,900 --> 01:31:30,610
Life found a way.

919
01:31:32,940 --> 01:31:37,570
- No. That's crazy. - You're out of your mind. He's absolutely out of his mind.

920
01:31:38,240 --> 01:31:40,410
- Wait. - What exactly would this mean?

921
01:31:40,530 --> 01:31:44,370
We're talking about a calculated risk, which is the only option left to us.

922
01:31:44,450 --> 01:31:48,920
We'll never find the command Nedry used. He's covered his tracks far too well.

923
01:31:49,420 --> 01:31:52,250
I think it's obvious now that he's not coming back.

924
01:31:52,380 --> 01:31:56,880
So, shutting down the entire system... Get somebody else. I won't do it.

925
01:31:56,970 --> 01:32:01,970
Shutting down the system is the only way to wipe out everything he did.

926
01:32:03,260 --> 01:32:06,890
Now, as I understand it, all the systems will then come back

927
01:32:07,060 --> 01:32:09,770
on their original start-up mode. Correct?

928
01:32:09,980 --> 01:32:13,270
Theoretically, yes. We've never shut down the entire system before.

929
01:32:13,400 --> 01:32:16,360
It may not come back on. Would we get the phones back?

930
01:32:16,440 --> 01:32:18,110
Yes, again, in theory.

931
01:32:18,740 --> 01:32:22,120
What about the lysine contingency? We could put that into effect.

932
01:32:22,240 --> 01:32:25,030
What's that? That's absolutely out of the question.

933
01:32:25,120 --> 01:32:27,950
The lysine contingency prevents the spread of animals,

934
01:32:28,080 --> 01:32:29,910
if they ever get off the island.

935
01:32:30,000 --> 01:32:33,670
Wu inserted a gene that creates a faulty enzyme in protein metabolism.

936
01:32:33,790 --> 01:32:36,670
The animals can't manufacture the amino acid, lysine.

937
01:32:36,800 --> 01:32:40,510
Unless they're supplied with lysine by us, they slip into a coma and die.

938
01:32:40,630 --> 01:32:43,090
People are dying.

939
01:32:47,310 --> 01:32:49,640
Will you please shut down the system?

940
01:33:11,660 --> 01:33:13,330
Hold on to your butts.

941
01:33:33,190 --> 01:33:34,310
It's okay.

942
01:33:34,440 --> 01:33:37,110
Look, see that? It's on. It worked.

943
01:33:39,610 --> 01:33:41,990
What do you mean it worked? Everything's off.

944
01:33:42,070 --> 01:33:46,200
Shutdown tripped the circuit breakers. Turn them back on, reboot a few systems:

945
01:33:46,280 --> 01:33:49,660
telephones, security doors, half dozen others, but it worked.

946
01:33:49,740 --> 01:33:51,830
System's ready. Where are the breakers?

947
01:33:51,910 --> 01:33:53,960
Maintenance shed at the end of the compound.

948
01:33:54,040 --> 01:33:56,790
Three minutes, I'll have the power back on in the park.

949
01:33:56,880 --> 01:33:59,960
Just to be safe, I want everybody in the emergency bunker

950
01:34:00,050 --> 01:34:03,380
until Mr. Arnold returns, and the whole system's running again.

951
01:34:03,680 --> 01:34:03,680
I'm tired. I'm dirty.

952
01:34:03,970 --> 01:34:05,130
I'm tired. I'm dirty.

953
01:34:05,220 --> 01:34:06,590
I'm hot.

954
01:34:06,800 --> 01:34:10,560
Looking at the map, I'd say the visitor's center is just a mile

955
01:34:11,220 --> 01:34:14,520
over that rise there. Just keep...

956
01:34:17,400 --> 01:34:18,900
What is that?

957
01:34:21,190 --> 01:34:23,400
Tim, can you tell me what they are?

958
01:34:24,780 --> 01:34:26,110
They are

959
01:34:30,450 --> 01:34:31,700
Gallimimus.

960
01:34:31,790 --> 01:34:34,290
Are those meat-eating?

961
01:34:35,920 --> 01:34:37,330
"Meat-asauruses"?

962
01:34:42,210 --> 01:34:44,670
Look at the wheeling. Uniform direction changes.

963
01:34:44,760 --> 01:34:47,430
Just like a flock of birds evading a predator.

964
01:34:48,930 --> 01:34:52,100
They're flocking this way.

965
01:35:35,060 --> 01:35:37,230
I want to go now. Just look how it eats.

966
01:35:37,310 --> 01:35:38,600
Please.

967
01:35:38,730 --> 01:35:41,480
I bet you'll never look at birds the same way again.

968
01:35:41,560 --> 01:35:43,650
Yes. Go now.

969
01:35:45,490 --> 01:35:48,150
Okay. Keep low and follow me.

970
01:35:50,570 --> 01:35:52,330
Look how much blood.

971
01:35:54,580 --> 01:35:56,660
God. Something went wrong.

972
01:35:57,580 --> 01:36:01,130
Something's happened. Something's wrong.

973
01:36:03,840 --> 01:36:05,420
This is just a delay.

974
01:36:05,510 --> 01:36:08,590
That's all it is. All major theme parks have delays.

975
01:36:08,840 --> 01:36:13,180
When they opened Disneyland in 1956, nothing worked.

976
01:36:13,600 --> 01:36:17,270
If the Pirates of the Caribbean breaks down, the pirates don't eat tourists.

977
01:36:17,350 --> 01:36:22,270
I can't wait any more. Something's wrong. I'm gonna go get the power back on.

978
01:36:22,520 --> 01:36:25,650
You can't just stroll down the road, you know?

979
01:36:25,820 --> 01:36:29,110
Don't let's be too hasty. I mean, it's only been gone...

980
01:36:31,780 --> 01:36:33,830
I'm going with you. Okay.

981
01:36:49,470 --> 01:36:50,680
Sorry.

982
01:36:54,510 --> 01:36:58,730
Now, this isn't going to be just like switching on the kitchen light.

983
01:36:58,890 --> 01:37:02,230
But I think I can follow this and then talk you through it.

984
01:37:06,690 --> 01:37:07,900
Right.

985
01:37:13,910 --> 01:37:15,910
But it ought to be me, really, going.

986
01:37:16,030 --> 01:37:18,910
Why? I'm a... And you're a...

987
01:37:20,370 --> 01:37:22,670
Look. Come on, let's go.

988
01:37:22,750 --> 01:37:26,000
We can discuss sexism in survival situations when I get back.

989
01:37:26,090 --> 01:37:29,760
You just take me through this step by step. I'm on Channel 2.

990
01:37:29,840 --> 01:37:30,880
Right.

991
01:38:06,750 --> 01:38:09,460
The shutdown must've turned off all the fences.

992
01:38:10,130 --> 01:38:13,800
Damn it, even Nedry knew better than to mess with the Raptor pen.

993
01:38:19,470 --> 01:38:20,720
Come on, this way.

994
01:38:28,440 --> 01:38:30,400
I can see the shed from here.

995
01:38:30,610 --> 01:38:32,320
We can make it if we run.

996
01:38:32,650 --> 01:38:35,240
No. We can't.

997
01:38:36,160 --> 01:38:37,450
Why not?

998
01:38:37,950 --> 01:38:39,870
Because we're being hunted.

999
01:38:41,200 --> 01:38:43,200
In the bushes, straight ahead.

1000
01:38:45,830 --> 01:38:47,170
It's all right.

1001
01:38:47,710 --> 01:38:49,130
Like hell it is.

1002
01:38:50,460 --> 01:38:53,630
Run. Towards the shed.

1003
01:38:55,840 --> 01:38:57,300
I've got her.

1004
01:38:58,220 --> 01:38:59,720
Go. Now!

1005
01:39:18,910 --> 01:39:20,320
Mr. Arnold?

1006
01:39:25,660 --> 01:39:26,870
John, I'm in.

1007
01:39:27,500 --> 01:39:28,710
Great.

1008
01:39:30,000 --> 01:39:33,500
Ahead of you is a metal staircase. Go down it.

1009
01:39:34,550 --> 01:39:36,840
Okay. Going down.

1010
01:39:37,720 --> 01:39:41,470
After 20 or 30 feet you come to a T-junction. Take a left.

1011
01:39:41,550 --> 01:39:44,720
Have her follow the main cable. I know how to read a schematic.

1012
01:40:15,050 --> 01:40:17,260
I guess that means the power's off.

1013
01:40:30,480 --> 01:40:33,110
That's not funny. That was great.

1014
01:40:35,610 --> 01:40:37,570
Well, maybe we, we could...

1015
01:40:55,420 --> 01:40:57,920
Damn it. Dead end.

1016
01:40:58,300 --> 01:40:59,510
Wait a minute.

1017
01:41:01,090 --> 01:41:04,350
There should have been a right turn back there somewhere.

1018
01:41:05,300 --> 01:41:06,930
Look above you.

1019
01:41:07,810 --> 01:41:11,640
There should be a bundle of cable and pipes all heading in the same direction.

1020
01:41:11,770 --> 01:41:12,940
Follow that.

1021
01:41:13,600 --> 01:41:15,770
Okay. Following the piping.

1022
01:41:18,440 --> 01:41:22,860
I bet I could climb over to the other side before you could even get to the top.

1023
01:41:22,990 --> 01:41:25,370
What would you give me? Respect.

1024
01:41:26,280 --> 01:41:28,330
Come on, guys, it's not a race.

1025
01:41:30,000 --> 01:41:31,210
I see the box.

1026
01:41:33,000 --> 01:41:36,000
It says, "High Voltage." Yeah.

1027
01:41:39,050 --> 01:41:40,210
Okay.

1028
01:41:44,180 --> 01:41:46,850
Good. Here we go.

1029
01:41:47,510 --> 01:41:48,680
Over the top.

1030
01:41:49,350 --> 01:41:50,980
Take your time.

1031
01:41:51,980 --> 01:41:53,520
Good. Come on.

1032
01:41:53,690 --> 01:41:55,650
Find your footing.

1033
01:41:57,860 --> 01:42:00,570
You can't throw the main switch by hand.

1034
01:42:00,690 --> 01:42:04,070
You've got to pump up the primer handle in order to get the charge.

1035
01:42:04,200 --> 01:42:06,530
It's large, flat, and gray.

1036
01:42:07,330 --> 01:42:09,200
All right, here I go. Okay?

1037
01:42:10,790 --> 01:42:15,880
One, two, three, four.

1038
01:42:16,330 --> 01:42:17,920
Okay, charged.

1039
01:42:18,670 --> 01:42:22,420
Under the words "Contact Position ," there's a round green button

1040
01:42:22,720 --> 01:42:25,050
which says "Push to Close."

1041
01:42:25,590 --> 01:42:27,430
Push to close.

1042
01:42:30,930 --> 01:42:32,220
Push it.

1043
01:42:47,160 --> 01:42:51,120
The red buttons turn on the individual park systems.

1044
01:42:51,990 --> 01:42:53,290
Switch them on.

1045
01:43:04,800 --> 01:43:07,010
Get down now! You're gonna have to jump.

1046
01:43:07,090 --> 01:43:08,930
You crazy? I'm not gonna jump.

1047
01:43:09,010 --> 01:43:11,640
Do what Dr. Grant says! Let go. I'll count to three.

1048
01:43:11,760 --> 01:43:14,140
One, two, three!

1049
01:43:15,100 --> 01:43:17,480
Four. Five.

1050
01:43:18,270 --> 01:43:19,980
I'm coming up to get you.

1051
01:43:20,110 --> 01:43:21,610
I've got to get Tim.

1052
01:43:21,770 --> 01:43:23,440
Okay. I'm gonna count to three.

1053
01:43:26,320 --> 01:43:27,530
One,

1054
01:43:29,280 --> 01:43:30,370
two...

1055
01:43:41,460 --> 01:43:42,960
He's not breathing.

1056
01:43:47,880 --> 01:43:50,300
I think we're back in business!

1057
01:43:58,520 --> 01:43:59,980
No!

1058
01:45:30,070 --> 01:45:31,320
Clever girl.

1059
01:45:55,640 --> 01:45:56,930
No, Tim!

1060
01:45:59,680 --> 01:46:01,600
Good boy.

1061
01:46:06,150 --> 01:46:07,360
Three.

1062
01:46:12,530 --> 01:46:13,610
Hello?

1063
01:46:23,790 --> 01:46:27,210
Okay. I'm gonna have to find the others.

1064
01:46:28,290 --> 01:46:31,050
Get you to a doctor.

1065
01:46:33,090 --> 01:46:35,380
Lex, you look after Tim. Yeah.

1066
01:46:36,680 --> 01:46:38,640
Your hair is all sticking up.

1067
01:46:40,640 --> 01:46:42,930
Big Tim, the human piece of toast.

1068
01:46:47,230 --> 01:46:49,400
I'll be back soon. I promise.

1069
01:47:16,720 --> 01:47:17,840
Run.

1070
01:48:34,340 --> 01:48:36,260
Just the two Raptors, right?

1071
01:48:37,760 --> 01:48:39,630
You sure the third one's contained?

1072
01:48:39,720 --> 01:48:43,300
Yes, unless they figure out how to open doors.

1073
01:49:09,910 --> 01:49:13,210
What is it? It's a Velociraptor.

1074
01:49:15,880 --> 01:49:17,380
It's inside.

1075
01:49:42,950 --> 01:49:44,030
Follow me.

1076
01:52:19,600 --> 01:52:20,850
It's in there.

1077
01:52:21,730 --> 01:52:22,980
Control room.

1078
01:52:29,320 --> 01:52:32,820
We can call for help? We've got to reboot the system first.

1079
01:52:35,450 --> 01:52:36,750
The door locks!

1080
01:52:37,660 --> 01:52:39,710
Ellie, boot up the door locks!

1081
01:52:49,220 --> 01:52:51,050
No, boot up the door locks!

1082
01:52:52,090 --> 01:52:55,930
Get back! Boot up the door locks. You can't hold it by yourself!

1083
01:53:04,360 --> 01:53:07,860
It's a UNIX system. I know this.

1084
01:53:08,610 --> 01:53:10,700
It's all the files of the whole park.

1085
01:53:10,780 --> 01:53:14,030
It tells you everything. I've got to find the right file.

1086
01:53:14,780 --> 01:53:16,370
Try to reach the gun.

1087
01:53:24,880 --> 01:53:26,840
I can't get it unless I move.

1088
01:53:42,560 --> 01:53:44,690
This is it. This might be the right file.

1089
01:54:00,870 --> 01:54:02,460
You got it! Yes!

1090
01:54:05,920 --> 01:54:07,170
Did it!

1091
01:54:07,420 --> 01:54:08,750
Yes!

1092
01:54:13,010 --> 01:54:14,220
What works?

1093
01:54:14,300 --> 01:54:17,010
All security systems are enabled. We got it.

1094
01:54:26,900 --> 01:54:28,110
Grant.

1095
01:54:28,190 --> 01:54:31,110
Mr. Hammond, the phones are working.

1096
01:54:31,610 --> 01:54:34,280
The children all right? The children are fine.

1097
01:54:34,780 --> 01:54:38,620
Call the mainland. Tell them to send the damn helicopters.

1098
01:54:39,410 --> 01:54:41,580
It's gonna cut through the glass!

1099
01:55:33,300 --> 01:55:34,460
Move!

1100
01:56:20,010 --> 01:56:22,550
Tim, let go. Yeah!

1101
01:57:39,920 --> 01:57:44,220
After careful consideration, I've decided not to endorse your park.

1102
01:57:44,970 --> 01:57:46,390
So have I.

1103
01:58:33,980 --> 01:58:35,020
Come on.

